# Cancel internal state without exiting

C-g cancels the innermost mode, then pending deletions, and otherwise does
nothing. C-c and Esc exit the picker without clearing persisted deletions.

    :bins jj tmux cat test grep

> [!NOTE]
> 'jj', 'tmux', 'cat', 'test', and 'grep' are available.

    :copy tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)

    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :$ jj git init alpha (exit: 0)

    :$ jj workspace add -R alpha --name feature alpha.feature (exit: 0)

    :t new-session -d -s ui "smth --base alpha -r 'alpha*' --query feature; tmux wait-for -S first-exited; cat" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 120 -y 12 (success)
    :pane ui:0.0
    :settle -d 2s -e '1/4' -e alpha/feature -e 'C-d. delete' (settled)

    :k C-p C-d
    :settle -d 2s -e '1 session' (settled)

    :snap

```terminal
session: feature                                                                                                       ┃
  1/4 | [C-r] repo: ~/alpha, [C-o] onto: trunk()                                                                       ┃
▌× alpha/feature                            ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-d] unstage                                                                      delete [C-y] 1 session [C-g] cancel┃
```

On a narrow terminal, the right-hand deletion controls take precedence over
session actions and the gap between them, even at extremely narrow widths.

    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 30 -y 4 (success)
    :snap

```terminal
session: feature             │
  1/4 | [C-r] repo: ~/alpha, │
▌× alpha/feature             │
delete [C-y] 1 session [C-g] ┃
```

    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 2 -y 4 (success)
    :snap

```terminal
se

▌×
de
```

    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 120 -y 12 (success)
    :settle -d 2s -e '1/4' -e alpha/feature -e '1 session' (settled)

Open onto mode over the staged deletion. C-g closes onto mode but leaves the
marker in place. A second C-g clears the marker, and a third keeps the app open.

    :k C-o
    :settle -d 2s -e '^onto:' (settled)

    :k C-g
    :settle -d 2s -e '^session:' -e '1 session' (settled)

    :snap

```terminal
session: feature                                                                                                       ┃
  1/4 | [C-r] repo: ~/alpha, [C-o] onto: trunk()                                                                       ┃
▌× alpha/feature                            ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-d] unstage                                                                      delete [C-y] 1 session [C-g] cancel┃
```

    :$ test -f alpha.feature/.jj/.smth-pending-delete (exit: 0)

    :k C-g
    :settle -d 2s -e alpha/feature -e 'C-d. delete' (settled)

    :snap

```terminal
session: feature                                                                                                       ┃
  1/4 | [C-r] repo: ~/alpha, [C-o] onto: trunk()                                                                       ┃
▌  alpha/feature                            ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-d] delete                                                                                                          ┃
```

    :$ test ! -f alpha.feature/.jj/.smth-pending-delete (exit: 0)

    :k C-g backspace
    :settle -d 2s -e '^session: featur\s' (settled)

    :k e
    :settle -d 2s -e '^session: feature\s' (settled)

    :snap

```terminal
session: feature                                                                                                       ┃
  1/4 | [C-r] repo: ~/alpha, [C-o] onto: trunk()                                                                       ┃
▌  alpha/feature                            ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-d] delete                                                                                                          ┃
```

Stage again and exit with C-c. The exit signal synchronizes the assertion that
the marker survived, and the restarted picker shows the selection again.

    :k C-d
    :settle -d 2s -e '1 session' (settled)

    :k C-c
    :t wait-for first-exited (success)

    :$ test -f alpha.feature/.jj/.smth-pending-delete (exit: 0)

    :t respawn-pane -k -t ui:0.0 "smth --base alpha -r 'alpha*' --query feature; tmux wait-for -S second-exited; cat" (success)
    :settle -d 2s -e '1/4' -e alpha/feature -e 'C-d. unstage' (settled)

    :k C-p
    :settle -d 2s -e '1 session' (settled)

    :snap

```terminal
session: feature                                                                                                       ┃
  1/4 | [C-r] repo: ~/alpha, [C-o] onto: trunk()                                                                       ┃
▌× alpha/feature                            ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-d] unstage                                                                      delete [C-y] 1 session [C-g] cancel┃
```

Esc exits even from onto mode, leaving the marker intact.

    :k C-o
    :settle -d 2s -e '^onto:' (settled)

    :k esc
    :t wait-for second-exited (success)

    :$ test -f alpha.feature/.jj/.smth-pending-delete (exit: 0)

C-c also exits from onto mode, rather than cancelling it.

    :t respawn-pane -k -t ui:0.0 "smth --base alpha -r 'alpha*' --query feature; tmux wait-for -S third-exited; cat" (success)
    :settle -d 2s -e '1/4' -e alpha/feature -e 'C-d. unstage' (settled)

    :k C-o
    :settle -d 2s -e '^onto:' (settled)

    :k C-c
    :t wait-for third-exited (success)

    :$ test -f alpha.feature/.jj/.smth-pending-delete (exit: 0)

Finally, Esc exits directly from session mode with the same persistence.

    :t respawn-pane -k -t ui:0.0 "smth --base alpha -r 'alpha*' --query feature; tmux wait-for -S fourth-exited; cat" (success)
    :settle -d 2s -e '1/4' -e alpha/feature -e 'C-d. unstage' (settled)

    :k esc
    :t wait-for fourth-exited (success)

    :$ test -f alpha.feature/.jj/.smth-pending-delete (exit: 0)

    :$ test -d alpha.feature (exit: 0)

